BOINC docker_wrapper: GPU access with Podman 4.x.

For apps with use_gpu the wrapper always adds "--gpus all". Podman only knows that
Docker option since version 5; Podman 4.x (e.g. 4.9.3 in Ubuntu 24.04 and Linux Mint 22)
fails with "Error: unknown flag: --gpus", so no container is created and the task
ends with exit code 1 after a few seconds.
With Podman the wrapper now requests the GPUs as CDI devices ("--device
nvidia.com/gpu=all"), which works with every Podman version with CDI support
(4.1 and newer) and needs the CDI specification created by "nvidia-ctk cdi generate".
Docker keeps "--gpus all".
Written for server_release/1.6/1.6.2 on top of 0002 and 0004.

diff --git a/samples/docker_wrapper/docker_wrapper.cpp b/samples/docker_wrapper/docker_wrapper.cpp
index ca2615f..94ed248 100644
--- a/samples/docker_wrapper/docker_wrapper.cpp
+++ b/samples/docker_wrapper/docker_wrapper.cpp
@@ -687,7 +687,14 @@ int create_container() {
     // GPU access
     //
     if (config.use_gpu) {
-        strcat(cmd, " --gpus all");
+        if (docker_type == PODMAN) {
+            // Podman < 5 has no --gpus (e.g. 4.9.3 in Ubuntu 24.04 / Linux Mint 22).
+            // CDI device names work with all Podman versions that support CDI (4.1+);
+            // needs the CDI spec from "nvidia-ctk cdi generate"
+            strcat(cmd, " --device nvidia.com/gpu=all");
+        } else {
+            strcat(cmd, " --gpus all");
+        }
     }
 
     // web graphics
